  28:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/max_torque_per_ampere.c **** /** @addtogroup STELLAR_PMSM_MC_FOC_LIBRARY
  29:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/max_torque_per_ampere.c ****   * @{
  30:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/max_torque_per_ampere.c ****   */
  31:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/max_torque_per_ampere.c **** 
  32:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/max_torque_per_ampere.c **** /** @defgroup MTPA Maximum Torque Per Ampere Control
  33:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/max_torque_per_ampere.c ****   * @brief Maximum Torque Per Ampere (MTPA) Control component of the Stellar Motor Control
  34:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/max_torque_per_ampere.c ****   *
  35:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/max_torque_per_ampere.c ****   *  The torque of the PMSM can be expressed with the equation shown below:
  36:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/max_torque_per_ampere.c ****   *
  37:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/max_torque_per_ampere.c ****   *  @f[
  38:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/max_torque_per_ampere.c ****   *  T_e = \frac{3}{2}\times p \times \phi \times i_q + \frac{3}{2}\times p\times(L_d-L_q)\times i_
  39:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/max_torque_per_ampere.c ****   *  @f]
  40:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/max_torque_per_ampere.c ****   *
  41:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/max_torque_per_ampere.c ****   *    When the motor is surface permanent magnet synchronous motor SPMSM the @f$ L_d @f$ and @f$ L
  42:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/max_torque_per_ampere.c ****   *  is almost same, so only the @f$ i_q @f$ can influence the torque. For internal permanent
  43:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/max_torque_per_ampere.c ****   *  magnet synchronous motor the @f$ L_d @f$  is not equel to @f$ L_q @f$. Both @f$ i_d @f$ and @f
  44:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/max_torque_per_ampere.c ****   *  the torque.
  45:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/max_torque_per_ampere.c ****   *    The aim of the MTPA (maximum-torque-per-ampere) control is to calculate the
  46:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/max_torque_per_ampere.c ****   *  reference currents (@f$ i_qs@f$ , @f$ i_ds@f$) which maximize the ratio between produced
  47:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/max_torque_per_ampere.c ****   *  electro-magnetic torque and copper losses.
  48:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/max_torque_per_ampere.c ****   *    Call this function after you get the @f$ I_q @f$  refernece.the input of this component
  49:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/max_torque_per_ampere.c ****   * is the @f$ i_q @f$  reference, the output of this component is @f$ i_d @f$ reference.
  50:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/max_torque_per_ampere.c ****   *
  51:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/max_torque_per_ampere.c ****   * @{
  52:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/max_torque_per_ampere.c ****   */
  53:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/max_torque_per_ampere.c **** 
